Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: ncz-screensavers
Source: https://gitlab.com/ncz-os/ncz-screensavers
Comment: The project is Apache-2.0. Each screensaver is a separate program, so
 the NCZ-authored glue and in-house engines are Apache-2.0 while every
 vendored or ported component keeps its own licence and notice. The
 per-component record is also in NOTICES.md, NOTICE and docs/PROVENANCE.tsv.

Files: *
Copyright: 2026 Jason Perlow and contributors
License: Apache-2.0
Comment: The Apache-2.0 grant covers only the original NCZ-authored code:
 the Wayland/EGL/GLES3 harness and drivers, the launcher, the idle timer, the
 Singularity plugin, the development tools, the tests, and the original
 in-house engines (Fractasia, Magmasimplex, Neonhorizon, Neonspacewar,
 Ephemeris, Megacity and Genxvectorcade). SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 headers mark those files. Every other file is covered by a more specific
 stanza below and retains its upstream licence.

Files: vendor/blackhole/* vendor/blackhole-LICENSE.txt src/gles3_blackhole.c
Copyright: 2015 Otto Seiskari
 2026 Adriwin
 2026 Jason Perlow and contributors
License: MIT
Comment: Port of Adriwin06/black-hole (MIT); upstream license text in
 vendor/blackhole-LICENSE.txt. The color-model work follows
 hydrogendeuteride/BlackHoleRayTracer (MIT) in method only. The upstream
 CC-BY-NC Milky Way texture is replaced by a procedural sky and is not used.

Files: vendor/hyprsaver/*
Copyright: 2026 Mara Vexa
License: MIT
Comment: Upstream license in vendor/hyprsaver/LICENSE; the individual shaders
 carry no header of their own. Four Fractasia families adapt hyprsaver
 shaders (see docs/fractasia/LICENSE-ANALYSIS.md).

Files: vendor/xshadertoy/glsl/*
Copyright: the individual shader authors named in each file header
License: MIT or CC0-1.0 or CC-BY-3.0
Comment: The ported shaders declare their own licence identifier in their
 header (MIT, CC0-1.0 or CC-BY-3.0); several are relicensed MIT by permission
 of the author. The CC0 shaders neontriangulator and neongravity-1 embedded
 helper snippets marked "License: Unknown"; in 0.8.9 those helpers were
 replaced with an Inigo Quilez MIT hash and an in-house filmic tone curve, so
 no unknown-licence snippet remains. stardome, selfreflect and stripeytorus
 remain excluded from the package for the same reason.

